                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238285292",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198828844317",
                            "num_reviews": 12,
                            "playtime_forever": 1359,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1359,
                            "last_played": 1791064170
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "By far one of my favorite souls games. But i only really liked Hellpoint, Bleak Faith, Steel Rising, Salt and Sanctuary, and Dark Souls 1. This is the only game that's kind of scratched my Hellpoint itch (the absolute best souls game imo once you figure it out).\n\nPeople complaining about the slow movement just have no common sense - the areas are so tiny that even if you move slow you still get from point A to point B faster than probably any other soulslike. You move about as fast as the Penitent one and nobody complains that Blasphemous is too slow. And I didn't encounter any bugs on my crappy computer.\n\nIt's a masterpiece of minimalism. It has just enough (and no more) of what makes a souls game force you to finish it, despite constant rage-quitting. I only found one secret though, so that is my only complaint: needs more secrets. Only took 22 hours. I still have to beat it in NG+, which changes things up enough to give you more abilities and surprises you with new enemies.\n\nYes, it's more difficult than I usually like games to be. Only 5% of people beat it. That makes it a worthy challenge. People seem to think that beating a souls game is some sort of badge of honour (as if video games are anyway near as difficult as real skills which take years to git gud at). So they like to mention all the souls games they've beaten in reviews and discussions. But beating this game in NG+ will be a real achievement since there's no guides or messages from other users to help you \"git gud\", you actually have to beat it on your own with no way to run past enemies to find better weapons and upgrade materials before going back to beat earlier bosses (like how people play fromsoft games).\n\nI suck at video games. Didn't start playing any until my 30's and had never even used a controller with thumb joysticks until this year, so if I can do it so can you. The vibes and animations and lore and weapons and powers are so perfect. If a boss is too difficult there's always other areas to go and explore - no farming neccessary :D I'm only giving a review because it deserves so much more. Really hoping for a sequel!",
